!TP_COMPRESSGAMUT_POWER_TOOLTIP;Power: Controls the aggressiveness of the compression curve.\n Higher power values result in more compressed values distributed closer to the gamut boundary. This will increase the "color purity" or "saturation" once the image has been rendered through a display transform.\n Higher values have a smoother transition.
