!TP_ICM_PRIMILLUM_TOOLTIP;You can change an image from its original mode ('working profile') to a different mode ('destination primaries'). When you choose a different color mode for an image, you permanently change the color values in the image.\n\nChanging the 'primaries' is quite complex and difficult to use. It requires a lot of experimenting.\n It is capable of making exotic color adjustments as Channel Mixer primaries.\n Allows you to modify the camera calibration with Custom (sliders).
!TP_ICM_PRIMREDROT_TOOLTIP;Change the Red, Green, and Blue primaries. The first slider rotates the primary color, in degrees, around the white point. The second increases or decreases the saturation relative to the white point.\n\nBe very careful when using this type of tool - whether it's polar sliders, linear sliders, or CIExy graphs. If you go outside the CIExy diagram, you'll generate imaginary colors, how will they be handled? If you reduce the primary values too much, you risk out-of-gamut data. Use with caution, and with small values, while monitoring the primaries' deviation from the CIExy diagram.
