!TP_LOCALLAB_PRECAM_TOOLTIP;Source Data Adjustments modifies the dynamic range (using log encoding), image tones (including midtones) and primaries (using a simplified Abstract Profile), just prior to the CIECAM process. The following parameters can be adjusted\nGamma: acts mainly on light tones\nSlope: acts mainly on dark tones. The algorithm ensures that there is continuity between the linear and parabolic parts of the curve for all combinations of gamma and slope (values >1) .\nDestination primaries: Allows you to adjust the destination primaries to restore or change the image color (saturation). The color balance is largely preserved when the Working Profile and ‘Destination primaries’ are similar. The Working Profile is not modified. You can also fine tune the primaries and illuminant (white-point). Moving a primary away from the white point reduces saturation and vice versa. Pay attention to the gamut.
